{"author":{"id":"746a4d30afc20b78119cb8ed7c194f988174fc252f0e9d9eb92022244ef86db3"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1779834931,"nonce":"hHxMOIukXG4RHat8zZzZvPcAA4s=","metadata":{"github-id":"IC_kwDOK4fCvM8AAAABDy1iNQ","github-url":"https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/163#issuecomment-4549599797"},"message":"## 2026-05-26 deployment ([#173](https://github.com/rolker/unh_echoboats_project11/issues/173)): probe produced good in-water data — keeping open as a watch item\n\nOn the 2026-05-26 BizzyBoat deployment the AML SVS produced **valid, stable sound-speed data in the water** — a complete turnaround from the 2026-05-22 all-NUL failure that opened this issue.\n\nIn-water window (12:48:54–14:08:40 EDT), `/bizzy/sensors/sound_speed/sound_speed`:\n- **98.8% valid readings** (117,961 / 119,346); only **1.2% zero-dropouts**.\n- Real values **1481.9–1491.0 m/s, median 1489.9** — plausible saltwater sound speed, with a small smooth **+0.74 m/s** rise over the hour (consistent with surface warming / water-mass change).\n- First valid reading ~19 s after launch (probe settling on water entry); the dropouts cluster in the first ~30 min, then the trace is rock-solid to recovery.\n- Pre-launch on the cart reads 0.0 (dry — expected).\n- Pre-deploy bench check: `minicom` confirmed data flowing on the serial line before launch.\n\nThe all-NUL behavior did **not** reproduce. **Keeping this issue open** for a few more deployments as a watch item rather than closing on a single good run — and to track the minor intermittent zero-dropouts (probe momentarily losing lock; feeds M3, which presumably holds last value) in case M3 sound-speed accuracy proves sensitive.\n\nDetail: #173 post-mission analysis (`docs/analysis/2026-05-26/findings.md` §5, landing via #182).\n\n---\n**Authored-By**: `Claude Code Agent`\n**Model**: `Claude Opus 4.7 (1M context)`","files":null}]}